# Microsoft Publisher Replacement Architecture Report

## Design Goal

Keep the existing DraftHouse Markdown, theme, page, and browser-print rendering engines intact. Add Microsoft Publisher-like editing through an absolute-positioned **page-object overlay** and structured brew metadata.

Do not rewrite:

- the Markdown/marked-hbfm rendering pipeline
- theme inheritance
- the iframe renderer
- page splitting
- browser print/PDF generation

## Least-Invasive Architecture

Render an additional object layer inside each existing page:

```text
.page
  .columnWrapper       # Existing Markdown output
  .pageObjectLayer     # Publisher-like positioned objects
  .guideLayer          # Edit-mode-only guides
```

The existing Markdown flow remains responsible for normal document text. The object layer is responsible for positioned images, text boxes, shapes, guides, and stacking.

## Core Extension Point

The main implementation point is [BrewRenderer](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/client/homebrew/brewRenderer/brewRenderer.jsx).

Add:

- a `PageObjectLayer` component
- a `PageObject` or generic object component
- page-index and edit-mode props
- pointer-drag and resize handling
- object sorting by `zIndex`

Keep `renderPage()` and `hbfm.render()` unchanged. Keep `BrewPage` as the page wrapper and add the object layer beside `columnWrapper`.

The iframe and page DOM are already isolated by `react-frame-component`, so visual editing can be contained in [BrewRenderer](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/client/homebrew/brewRenderer/brewRenderer.jsx) and its CSS.

## Styling Extension Point

Add additive styles to [brewRenderer.less](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/client/homebrew/brewRenderer/brewRenderer.less):

- `.page { position: relative; }`
- `.pageObjectLayer { position: absolute; inset: 0; pointer-events: none; }`
- `.pageObject { position: absolute; pointer-events: auto; }`
- selection handles
- hover and locked states
- guide and grid styles

Keep the existing page dimensions:

```text
215.9mm x 279.4mm
```

Object coordinates should use millimeters or percentages. Millimeters align most closely with existing print dimensions.

Hide guides, selection handles, and editing affordances under `@media print`.

## Draggable Images

Implement image objects as absolute DOM elements rather than changing Markdown image syntax.

Example object:

```text
{
  id: "image-1",
  page: 1,
  type: "image",
  layer: 3,
  x: "25mm",
  y: "30mm",
  width: "80mm",
  height: "50mm",
  rotation: "0deg",
  src: "/assets/example.png"
}
```

Relevant files:

- [BrewRenderer](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/client/homebrew/brewRenderer/brewRenderer.jsx)
- [brewRenderer.less](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/client/homebrew/brewRenderer/brewRenderer.less)
- [Editor](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/client/homebrew/editor/editor.jsx)
- [SnippetBar](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/client/homebrew/editor/snippetbar/snippetbar.jsx)

The existing image-mask snippets remain backward compatible:

- [imageMask.gen.js](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/themes/V3/Blank/snippets/imageMask.gen.js)
- [Legacy snippets.js](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/themes/Legacy/5ePHB/snippets.js)

Positioned image objects can be introduced as a new opt-in mode rather than replacing existing Markdown images.

## Text Boxes

Store text boxes as positioned objects:

```text
{
  id: "text-1",
  page: 2,
  type: "text",
  layer: 2,
  x: "25mm",
  y: "40mm",
  width: "90mm",
  height: "30mm",
  content: "## Heading\n\nText..."
}
```

In edit mode:

- use `contentEditable` or a small textarea overlay
- update the object model on input
- provide selection and resize handles

In view/preview mode:

- render the content with the existing `marked-hbfm` parser
- optionally support the existing Legacy parser for Legacy documents

Relevant files:

- [BrewRenderer](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/client/homebrew/brewRenderer/brewRenderer.jsx)
- [CodeEditor](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/client/components/codeEditor/codeEditor.jsx)
- [helpers.js](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/shared/helpers.js)
- [markdownLegacy.js](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/shared/markdownLegacy.js)

Do not initially add a new text-box Markdown syntax. Store boxes in structured metadata and optionally add a `{{textbox}}` syntax later.

## Positioned Shapes

Render shapes through the same generic object layer:

```text
{
  id: "shape-1",
  page: 1,
  type: "shape",
  shape: "rectangle",
  layer: 1,
  x: "10mm",
  y: "20mm",
  width: "50mm",
  height: "20mm",
  fill: "#ffffff",
  stroke: "#000000",
  strokeWidth: "1px",
  radius: "2mm"
}
```

Initial supported shapes should include:

- rectangle
- ellipse
- rounded rectangle
- line
- arrow
- divider

Relevant files:

- [BrewRenderer](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/client/homebrew/brewRenderer/brewRenderer.jsx)
- [brewRenderer.less](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/client/homebrew/brewRenderer/brewRenderer.less)

This does not require theme or Markdown changes.

## Page Guides

Guides should be viewer-only and should never be included in printed page content.

Add a guide layer above the object layer in edit mode:

- vertical guides
- horizontal guides
- margin guides
- grid guides
- custom guides
- snap-to-guide
- snap-to-grid

Example settings:

```text
{
  page: 1,
  guides: {
    grid: "5mm",
    vertical: ["25mm", "190mm"],
    horizontal: ["25mm", "254mm"],
    snap: true
  }
}
```

Relevant files:

- [BrewRenderer](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/client/homebrew/brewRenderer/brewRenderer.jsx)
- [brewRenderer.less](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/client/homebrew/brewRenderer/brewRenderer.less)
- [ToolBar](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/client/homebrew/brewRenderer/toolBar/toolBar.jsx)
- [ToolBar CSS](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/client/homebrew/brewRenderer/toolBar/toolBar.less)

The guide controls fit naturally into the existing toolbar.

## Layers

Add `layer` and `zIndex` fields to every object.

Render objects sorted in ascending stacking order:

```text
const orderedObjects = pageObjects
  .filter((object) => object.page === pageIndex)
  .sort((a, b) => a.zIndex - b.zIndex);
```

Initial layer operations:

- bring to front
- send to back
- move forward
- move backward
- show/hide
- lock/unlock

Relevant files:

- [BrewRenderer](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/client/homebrew/brewRenderer/brewRenderer.jsx)
- [Editor](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/client/homebrew/editor/editor.jsx)
- [brewRenderer.less](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/client/homebrew/brewRenderer/brewRenderer.less)

No theme or existing layout behavior needs to change.

## Data and Persistence

Add one primary brew field:

```text
pageObjects
```

Recommended default:

```text
pageObjects: []
```

Update persistence surfaces:

- [brewDefaults.js](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/server/brewDefaults.js)
- [homebrew.model.js](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/server/homebrew.model.js)
- [helpers.js](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/shared/helpers.js)
- [MetadataEditor](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/client/homebrew/editor/metadataEditor/metadataEditor.jsx)
- [homebrew.api.js](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/server/homebrew.api.js)

The existing autosave and save pipeline will require only additive field handling:

- include `pageObjects` in the client brew snapshot
- include it in patch/save payloads
- include it in default brew values
- preserve it when merging with Google and MongoDB storage
- include it in `mergeBrewText()` or store it separately in metadata

Prefer storing `pageObjects` as a dedicated structured field for the first implementation. An optional metadata block export can be added later.

## Existing Components to Reuse

- [EditorPage](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/client/homebrew/pages/basePages/editPage/editorPage.jsx)
  - already owns brew state and autosave
- [BrewRenderer](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/client/homebrew/brewRenderer/brewRenderer.jsx)
  - already owns page boundaries and iframe rendering
- [SnippetBar](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/client/homebrew/editor/snippetbar/snippetbar.jsx)
  - suitable for object insertion controls
- [ToolBar](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/client/homebrew/brewRenderer/toolBar/toolBar.jsx)
  - suitable for guide and zoom controls
- [MetadataEditor](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/client/homebrew/editor/metadataEditor/metadataEditor.jsx)
  - suitable for document layout settings
- [printCurrentBrew](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/shared/helpers.js)
  - continue using the existing browser print flow

## Print and PDF Behavior

Do not replace or fork [printCurrentBrew](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/shared/helpers.js).

Continue to:

1. prepare lazy images
2. wait for image loading
3. call `window.frames.BrewRenderer.contentWindow.print()`
4. let the browser print/Save as PDF

Print CSS in [brewRenderer.less](/home/ablc/projects/homebrewery/client/homebrew/brewRenderer/brewRenderer.less) will hide:

- toolbar
- header navigation
- guides
- selection handles

Object elements remain and print using their absolute positions.

## Recommended Implementation Order

1. Add `pageObjects: []` to the brew defaults and schema.
2. Add a generic absolute object layer to `BrewPage`.
3. Add positioned shape objects.
4. Add positioned text-box objects.
5. Add image insertion and drag/resize handles.
6. Add guide and grid rendering.
7. Add snapping and alignment controls.
8. Add a layer panel and stacking controls.
9. Optionally export objects into a metadata block.
